WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.616 --> 00:00:13.950
PRESENTER: Yes,
welcome, and thank you

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.620
all for coming to the third
lecture of our Fall lecture

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.200
series, God and Computers,
Minds, Machines, and

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.700
Metaphysics.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.430
I first, like always, would
like to thank our sponsors.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.260
I specifically would
like to mention

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.750
the Electrical Engineering
and Computer Science

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.280
Department at MIT.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:34.080
And also the Sir John Templeton
Foundation, and the rest of our

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.120
sponsors you can
find on the website.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.350
And I put them this
time on both sides.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.380
So if you want to
visit the websites,

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.030
you will find the abstracts
of the past talks,

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.050
and future talks,
and also some links.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.000
In the first lecture
of this series,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.380
we heard Paul Penfield, the head
of the Electrical Engineering

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.380
Computer Science
Department here at MIT,

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:59.010
talking about the character
of scientific theories.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.410
He expressed his
personal opinion,

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.470
that science would
not be completely

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:08.520
sufficient to describe what
he called the human factor.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.120
His examples were love, and
grief, and other things.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.910
Last week, this
very human factor

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:18.600
was described by Marc
Hauser from Harvard

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.900
from a comparative
ethology perspective.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:26.520
So he said that animals,
particularly monkeys and apes,

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.640
share several of these
human factors with humans.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.570
Like self-awareness, or
the notion of belief.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.540
And they also can
develop rituals.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:42.820
However, he said that they lack
the notion of moral agency.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.600
Today, now, we will hear
about another aspect

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.550
of the human factor from
a psychiatric perspective.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.740
And I'm very pleased
and very honored

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.310
to welcome Professor
Ming Tsuang here today.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.490
Professor Tsuang is currently
head of the Harvard Medical

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.940
School department of Psychiatry
at the Massachusetts Mental

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.600
Health Center.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.350
And he is also director
of the Harvard Institute

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.170
of Psychiatric
Epidemiology and Genetics.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:15.690
He's internationally known for
his research on schizophrenia,

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.390
and also other mental disorders.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.140
He holds an MD, a PhD, and
a doctorate of science,

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.360
and several honorary degrees.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.750
And besides numerous
awards and honors,

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.240
he's a member of the
National Academy of Science,

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.470
a member of the Acadamia
Sinica of Taiwan,

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:38.160
and he also just received the
Lifetime Achievement Award

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.510
from the International Society
of Psychiatric Genetics.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:47.520
Among his interests is
spirituality, with its effect

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.500
on mental disorders.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.150
And I'm really,
really glad that you

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.070
are now here to share with us
your ideas on the brain, mind

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.540
and spirituality.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.040
Welcome.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:04.672
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:04.672 --> 00:03:07.490
TSUANG: It is an honor.

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:10.600
And thank you very much
for inviting me here.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:16.790
Today I'm going to discuss
with you our brain, and mind,

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.790
and spirituality.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:22.630
I'd like to start off with
the brain, and then the brain

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:26.140
function, and the
mind, and then go

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.890
into how to tackle
the spirituality

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:34.460
from the epidemiological
point of view.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:39.810
So let's start with
the first slide.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.230
You can you see it from there?

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.810
It's the mind and the brain.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:52.390
Essential to understand
the mental process that,

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.520
essentially, has
changed dramatically

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.770
throughout the human history.

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.260
The heart, liver,
and other organs

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.270
were believed to be the
key to mental functions.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:08.050
Particularly from Chinese
traditional medicine,

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:12.220
still consider a
liver, and kidney,

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:17.470
and the other sexual organs seem
to be playing an important role

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:21.940
in the mental function,
and physical functions.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:28.585
And let us talk about the
ancient Greeks' concept.

00:04:28.585 --> 00:04:34.380
All living things drew vitality
from pneuma, essentially air,

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.400
derived from the cosmos.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.887
And then, so this is
related to Chinese Tai

00:04:40.887 --> 00:04:45.260
chi, and the various
kind of yin and yang.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.200
And growth,
movement, and thought

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.980
were caused by alteration
in this cosmos, pneuma.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:57.800
And the liver, essentially,
is the natural spirit.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:01.100
Heart is considered
to be vital spirit.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.760
And brain, animal spirit.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.230
All participated.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:09.500
This is the ancient
Greeks' concept.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:14.270
And the modern scientific view,
from 16th and 17th century,

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:17.780
the concept of nervous
system being developed.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:19.850
And essentially,
brain and spinal

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:23.900
cord being considered as
central to the function

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.330
to the nervous system.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:30.020
And peripheral nervous
system is essentially

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:36.540
nerves throughout the
body, which are actually,

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:40.990
essentially, under the direction
of central nervous system.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:44.060
So center is in the brain.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:47.110
And so just to give
you, for those who are--

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:50.410
I know there are several
eminent neuroscientists here--

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:54.580
forgive me in giving
the elementary brain

00:05:54.580 --> 00:06:00.050
structure for those who
have not seen the brain.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:02.370
Unlike some of the
neuroscientists

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:05.350
that are dealing
with this every day.

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:08.090
So essentially,
this is the brain.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:12.070
And we have a cranial
bone, which protects us.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:17.620
And you have a dura, an
arachnoid, and pia maters.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:22.660
If you have a concussion, you
may have a bleeding inside

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:28.660
of the dura, under dura
mater, subdural hematoma,

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.030
and various kind of conditions.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.420
And this cerebral
spinal fluid, this

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.790
is just to give you our brain.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:42.670
And the brain, somehow, has
the very important demarcation

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.050
for anatomist.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.910
And the neurophysiologist.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.620
And the neurochemist.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:50.920
To really point out
which part to study.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.440
So the frontal lobe--

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:56.770
I thank you to have this for me.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:00.700
So frontal lobe is here,
and then the prefrontal.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:04.040
These, and the
primordial cortex.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.690
So this is very important.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:11.290
I'm going to elaborate the mind,
mental function, and the brain.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:15.520
And this is the marking,
called Sylvian fissure.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:19.540
And under which is temporal
lobe, and the parietal lobe.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.730
And the sensory cortex is here.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:26.170
And here is a demarcation,
it's called central sulcus.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.090
And occipital lobe.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:33.360
And in what way this is
related to our mental function?

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:36.430
The major external brain
structure, as I showed you,

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:41.040
frontal lobe is the
executive function.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.560
Doing things, thinking
about the things,

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.570
and the planning for the future.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:50.040
And temporal lobe is
the auditory processing,

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.610
and related to language.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:55.350
Of course, you see the frontal
lobe also involved in language.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:58.750
And parietal lobe,
this is the summary

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.570
of what we know,
touch, and balance.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:05.680
And occipital lobe, in the
back, is related to vision.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:13.210
And brainstem is inducing the
sleep, arousal, heart rate,

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:16.040
and breathing.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:21.100
So these are, essentially,
the brain structure

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.610
and the functions.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:30.430
So let us see from this
side, the frontal lobe, then

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:32.450
parietal lobe, as
I talk about, then

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:35.460
the temporal lobe,
occipital lobe in the back,

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:36.760
and the brain stem.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:40.080
This is the vital organ.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.360
Vital, very vital,
to our survival.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:48.540
So even without this
part, if this is unhurt,

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.100
still we can survive.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:54.750
And respiration, heart rate,
are controlled by this area.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:59.510
And cerebellum is related
to balance and the movement.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:07.690
So from outside which you
can see, for us to discuss

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.010
the brain function.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:15.060
and the mind, we need to
know the major internal brain

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:15.560
structures.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:17.630
So hypothalmus.

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:22.960
This is related to our thirst,
hunger, and sexual function.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.460
Cerebellum is the
balance and movement.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:29.780
And corpus callosum connects
the two cerebral hemispheres.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:33.080
And thalamus is
important relay station

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:36.500
for sensory processing relay.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:39.830
So in this sense, you
can see already, here,

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:41.960
the inside, as I
already talked about,

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:46.730
corpus callosum, which connects
the two sides of the brain.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.870
We have a left side
and right side.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:52.070
And these two are
very symmetrical.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.670
One side can really function.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:59.180
We know from some of the
patients, even losing one side,

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.780
still can survive.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:03.040
And so, this is the
corpus callosum.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.770
And then I talk about
the hypothalamus.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:10.580
And this is the pituitary gland.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:14.160
And then the pineal gland.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.690
And the thalamus is here.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:17.480
Thalamus.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:20.810
And the medulla, this
is the brain stem.

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:23.000
Midbrain pons, and cerebellum.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:27.240
So this is just to give you
some of the brain structure.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:30.260
And another important
thing in mental function

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:34.070
from a psychiatric point
of view is the emotion.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.720
How you feel.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:41.740
And the limbic system controls
emotion, and memory, and also

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.470
all functions.

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:46.520
And this is the
limbic system inside.

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:48.650
So hypothalamus,
olfactory valve tract,

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.520
they are connected to this.

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:56.030
And mammilary bodies--
in some dementia

00:10:56.030 --> 00:11:00.510
due to alcoholism, mammilaries
tend to have bleeding.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:04.550
And amygdala, and hippocampus,
and fornix, and thalamus.

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:09.980
This is actually consisting
of the important structure

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.540
for our emotions.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:15.880
And the various important
function of mind.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:26.920
And then, there are various
nucleus within the brain.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.890
And this is the coded nucleus.

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:33.640
And the putamen,
caudate, and the globus

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.830
pallidus substantia negra.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:38.690
This is related to
Parkinson's, and so on.

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:41.900
And the reason I show
this is that, in the past,

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:45.970
we thought that this has nothing
to do with the mental function.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:51.100
But now we know, these are
also related very specifically

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.650
with the schizophrenia
research, which we are doing.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:57.460
So I'd just like to
introduce very quickly

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:03.130
the anatomical structure,
for us to understand

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.600
what I'm going to talk about.

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:07.820
So this is on the
anatomical level.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:16.040
But within the brain,
there are many, many cells

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.620
we call neurons.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:21.840
And neurons have a
nucleus and an axon,

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.080
and with myelin sheath.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:26.180
Covered with the axons.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:31.970
And then, are connected with
synapse to another neuron.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:37.670
So neuron has the axon, and
also has a dendrite, to connect.

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:42.540
One cell to connect to another
is actually very important.

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:46.820
So this is the two neurons
in synoptic contact.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:52.280
And this neural
network is the, as I

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:56.060
showed you, is the signal
transmission from one

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.890
neuron to another.

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:01.370
And it's been done
electrochemically.

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:06.140
And so, a nerve cell fires, then
signals go to the next neuron,

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.300
and small white
nodes are synapses.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.840
Gap between cells.

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:12.500
In the case of multiple
sclerosis, those are--

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:17.960
the one which I showed
you, that myelin sheath has

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:23.300
been affected, so that it
sort of, say, the electricity

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:27.260
is not efficiently passed on.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:31.290
So there is the
movement disorder.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:37.450
So this is the very important
function of the mind.

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:41.000
In order for a two to connect.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.920
And now, I'd like to talk
about the brain development.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:49.610
A human being is unique,
and I'd like to show you

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:50.990
the brain development.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:57.920
How it develops to have you,
now, with the mature brain.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:01.720
Brain develops beginning in
the first months in utero.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:05.450
And neurons migrate to
genetically pre-planned

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.780
regions, which is
very important.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:11.150
That cells migrate from
the bottom to the top,

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.470
to the cortex.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:17.540
The maximum neural migration
at the middle trimester.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:22.550
So the migration
may be affected in

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:27.710
the second or first trimester
by virus, or malnutrition,

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:28.770
or trauma.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:31.940
It may affect the brain
cells, the configuration.

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:36.200
That is what I'm going
to talk to you about.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:42.560
The current theory of
neurodevelopmental malfunction

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.723
of the brain, leading
to schizophrenia.

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:54.690
Am I standing here,
can you see it?

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:56.800
If I go there, they cannot see.

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:59.100
So there's no way.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.760
So I should stand here.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:01.260
OK.

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:02.350
Neural migration.

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:04.560
This now becomes very important.

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:08.400
Schizophrenia, once upon a
time thought as the possession

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.690
by devil.

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.190
At that time, we didn't know.

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:14.730
So ascribe everything
to those superstitions.

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:19.560
But now, with the new
development in neuroscience,

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:24.210
we now know that neural
migration is very important.

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:27.310
Neurons migrate in a
highly organized fashion.

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:29.160
Is the pre-plan.

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:35.040
But as I say, a virus,
genetically malformation,

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.530
may affect this
neuron migration.

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:40.590
The earliest migrants
from initial deep layer

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:45.540
later arrive and assume places
closer to the cortical surface.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:49.410
So just to illustrate
to you, those

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:53.480
are the all in the
superventricular,

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:58.670
or ventricular cells, migrate to
the top in the cortical plate,

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:03.980
where our thinking, our
feeling, and everything is

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:04.920
very important.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:06.450
Executive function.

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:08.940
So migration.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:13.830
And the earlier ones stop
here, but the later ones

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.830
come to the top.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:19.760
And sometimes,
there is the order

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:24.810
to ask some of those older
ones to die, in order

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:28.650
to save the younger
ones, to go to the top.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.480
so it's very interesting
that the brain

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.000
is wired in that sense.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.390
So all the cells, the
new ones, actually

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:37.500
come to the top layers.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:45.270
So this development
differentiates us

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:51.550
from other types of creatures.

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:56.640
This, developed by Paul
MacLean, represents the brain

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:59.670
in evolutionary terms.

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:04.569
From reptilian brainstem,
survival, respiration,

00:17:04.569 --> 00:17:07.980
heart rate, and the mammalian,
limbic, with the emotional .

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:12.060
System and the
neomammalian, actually

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:14.220
cortex for our cognition.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.740
So just to give you
some illustration.

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:21.960
This is the reptilian, and
this is the limbic system.

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:25.819
And then, neomammalian,
this is us,

00:17:25.819 --> 00:17:29.460
representing the greater
area of the cortex.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:32.840
And the cells all
migrate to the cortex.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:38.910
And there, you can see,
they're well arranged, and well

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:44.290
connected from one neuron to
another, for their function.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:48.940
So the important area which
has been discovered by Broca.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:52.910
Is the Brocas area,
named after Paul Broca.

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:55.850
French neurologist
of the 19th century.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:58.450
And it's essentially
our speech center.

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:01.740
Is at the left,
inferior, frontal lobe.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:05.020
And essential for
linguistic fluency.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:08.620
And if you have a
stroke, then if this area

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:12.090
is affected on the left side,
if you are right-hand side,

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:15.940
a person, left side affected,
then you have aphasia.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.240
You cannot speak.

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:20.200
So this is the Brocas area.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.170
This area.

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:27.600
And so in terms of the
brain and the mind,

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:31.320
the brain is well
integrated so that we

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:35.550
can do whatever you like to do.

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:39.270
In terms of thinking,
in terms of feeling,

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:40.760
in terms of your behavior.

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:45.000
It's totally integrated with
the brain, and the spinal cord,

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.130
and peripheral nervous system.

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:51.820
And what we recently
found was that

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:55.300
in schizophrenia, which
was originally considered

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:57.550
to be possessed by the devil.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:00.250
So you can hear the voices,
which is devil voices.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:02.500
You believe someone
is going to harm you.

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:06.430
And that kind of
abnormal behavior

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:12.710
was thought of as
the aberration.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:15.050
Because of the
possession by the devil.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.000
But recently, with the
neuroscience development,

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.850
we know that--

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:24.440
I'm going to show
you the PET scanning,

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:28.070
I show you that the normal
brain is on the left.

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:30.780
And the brain of the person with
schizophrenia is on the right.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:34.430
The schizophrenic brain
demonstrates lower blood flow.

00:19:34.430 --> 00:19:38.220
We can test the blood
flow in the frontal lobe.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:43.820
So essentially, you can see that
the normal, and the abnormal,

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:46.820
you can see the blood
flow is different.

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:51.050
Because the cell
configuration is different.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:55.580
So another one, I'm showing
you normal brain on top.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:57.100
Schizophrenic brain
in the middle.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:59.470
Then, with the drug
treatment, all the brain

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:01.300
function in schizophrenia.

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:04.980
So this, also, we can now
see from the PET scanner.

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:10.030
Normal, and the schizophrenia,
and after application

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:11.800
of the neuroleptics.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:15.220
Which treat the symptoms
of schizophrenia.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:18.490
And this, now, we can
show from PET scanners.

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:21.580
So essentially, to
give you a summary,

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:26.420
in psychiatry when we
examine the mental function,

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.900
these are the three
cardinal aspects--

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:31.120
we call mental status--

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.110
we examine.

00:20:32.110 --> 00:20:36.520
And to characterize, what
is the function of the mind.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:38.410
Mind cannot be seen.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:43.450
But as a psychiatrist,
we see the mind

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:46.440
when mind is functioning.

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:51.670
And three-dimensional approach
to the mental function is the,

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:54.940
you think, you feel,
and you behave.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:58.840
And these three, all of
us are well integrated.

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:07.000
So when you think about the
happy events, you are feeling.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.310
Feel high.

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:12.580
And you become sort of
elated and restless.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:17.240
So these are the
congress functions.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:21.570
However, in the case of
mania, it's a hyperfunction.

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:26.020
You have lots of ideas, and
you feel that you are so great.

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:27.937
You become the President
of the United States.

00:21:27.937 --> 00:21:30.145
These days, become the
President of the United States

00:21:30.145 --> 00:21:31.480
is not as good as before.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:36.910
[LAUGHTER] And you
are overactive.

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:38.920
So that is the mania.

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:43.040
And the depression is the
hypofunction of these three.

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:46.060
So however, these three
functions are congress.

00:21:46.060 --> 00:21:50.500
In schizophrenia-- this
is just for illustration.

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:54.520
In schizophrenia, these three
functions of mind, something

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:55.480
happened here.

00:21:55.480 --> 00:22:00.460
And current theory is that,
brain functions are disturbed.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:07.220
So when you believe that
people are trying to harm you,

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:14.780
yet your expression is
apathetic, not fearful.

00:22:14.780 --> 00:22:19.830
And then, you are
supposed to run,

00:22:19.830 --> 00:22:22.620
because someone is
trying to harm you.

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:25.410
But this person
sits there still.

00:22:25.410 --> 00:22:28.110
So this is the concept
of schizophrenia.

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:33.330
Different from mania
and depression.

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:36.580
So our study, during
the last 30 years,

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:42.050
our group are trying to find
what are the potential risk

00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:46.760
factors affecting the brain
for this cerebral function

00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:49.010
to become incongruous.

00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:54.570
So essentially, what I'm
saying is that, schizophrenia

00:22:54.570 --> 00:22:56.580
is no longer the myth.

00:22:56.580 --> 00:23:00.090
It's a brain disorder.

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:03.230
And we are now trying
to tackle, what are

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:05.130
the genetic components of it.

00:23:05.130 --> 00:23:08.010
What are the
environmental components--

00:23:08.010 --> 00:23:12.320
particularly intra-uterine
condition, and after birth--

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:15.140
in what way the
environment actually

00:23:15.140 --> 00:23:21.840
interacts with the
congenital malformation.

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:29.070
So our group, in collaboration
with the Mass General

00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:32.520
Neuroimaging, we
showed that this

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:37.860
is a normal control of the
normal person, volunteer.

00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:40.230
In the case of
schizophrenic patients,

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:45.480
lateral ventricle
becomes bigger.

00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:48.130
And inferior lateral
ventricles are bigger.

00:23:48.130 --> 00:23:50.440
Because their brains shrink.

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:55.380
Essentially, the cortex and the
other area of the brain volume

00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:56.800
decreases.

00:23:56.800 --> 00:23:58.840
So the lateral
ventricle, where we

00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:02.800
are supposed to have our
cerebral spinal fluid occupy

00:24:02.800 --> 00:24:04.580
there, is more.

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:08.290
So this is the indication of
the brain becoming smaller.

00:24:08.290 --> 00:24:13.270
And not only that, thalamus,
or lateral ventricle,

00:24:13.270 --> 00:24:15.460
is actually wider.

00:24:15.460 --> 00:24:18.520
And these thalamus, which
I've already shown to you,

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:21.700
putamen, pallidum,
hippocampus, amygdala complex.

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:25.570
This is all related to
feeling and emotion.

00:24:25.570 --> 00:24:28.420
Smaller than normal control.

00:24:28.420 --> 00:24:31.210
Now the research which
we are doing is this.

00:24:33.800 --> 00:24:42.050
Not only we are studying
schizophrenia patients,

00:24:42.050 --> 00:24:45.800
we are now studying the
relatives of schizophrenia.

00:24:45.800 --> 00:24:47.510
Where we are doing
the collection

00:24:47.510 --> 00:24:50.210
of DNA, and to test the genes.

00:24:50.210 --> 00:24:52.770
But to capitalize
on that opportunity,

00:24:52.770 --> 00:24:59.360
we compare the relatives who
are not schizophrenia yet.

00:24:59.360 --> 00:25:05.030
Still they show differences,
comparing with normal.

00:25:05.030 --> 00:25:07.805
Essentially, I
show you these are

00:25:07.805 --> 00:25:12.590
the areas which have been
affected even in the relatives.

00:25:12.590 --> 00:25:15.230
So it means that,
in the past, we

00:25:15.230 --> 00:25:23.840
don't know when to
intervene, to prevent

00:25:23.840 --> 00:25:26.400
the onset of schizophrenia.

00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:29.480
Now we know the earlier
treatment, the better.

00:25:29.480 --> 00:25:31.850
And even better is
before the treatment,

00:25:31.850 --> 00:25:35.030
if we can find
cognitive deficit.

00:25:35.030 --> 00:25:37.400
And the neuroimaging
abnormalities.

00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:40.430
We may be able to prevent them.

00:25:40.430 --> 00:25:42.860
So this is our work.

00:25:42.860 --> 00:25:47.190
So in addition to that,
we use the functional MRI.

00:25:47.190 --> 00:25:49.940
The control comparing with
relatives of schizophrenia.

00:25:49.940 --> 00:25:52.130
And of course, us the
schizophrenia is like this.

00:25:52.130 --> 00:25:54.140
But this is the milder.

00:25:54.140 --> 00:25:56.990
Essentially, for the
normal, you don't

00:25:56.990 --> 00:26:02.990
need to use so much energy
to do the assigned tasks.

00:26:02.990 --> 00:26:05.690
In schizophrenia,
and the relatives,

00:26:05.690 --> 00:26:08.750
because their brain
cells are arranged

00:26:08.750 --> 00:26:11.090
in such an inefficient
way, they have

00:26:11.090 --> 00:26:18.049
to utilize so much brain areas
to perform the same function

00:26:18.049 --> 00:26:18.715
as the controls.

00:26:21.370 --> 00:26:26.240
So current, very
strong hypothesis,

00:26:26.240 --> 00:26:32.430
and with scientific evidence, is
the neurodevelopmental models.

00:26:32.430 --> 00:26:35.250
These propose that
there's some combination

00:26:35.250 --> 00:26:38.160
of genetic and
non-genetic areas,

00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:42.390
leads to maldevelopment
of the brain in childhood.

00:26:42.390 --> 00:26:45.880
And we can see that
neuropsychological abnormality

00:26:45.880 --> 00:26:48.300
in children of
schizophrenic patient.

00:26:48.300 --> 00:26:51.360
And the obstetrical
complication in birth

00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:55.470
of schizophrenic
patient all impact

00:26:55.470 --> 00:27:00.180
to result into a
schizophrenic brain.

00:27:00.180 --> 00:27:05.190
And therefore, brain
and mind, is normal,

00:27:05.190 --> 00:27:06.870
it's well integrated.

00:27:06.870 --> 00:27:08.910
In schizophrenia,
which is the area

00:27:08.910 --> 00:27:11.280
of our research
for a long time, we

00:27:11.280 --> 00:27:16.170
feel that we can
really study brain

00:27:16.170 --> 00:27:18.390
to identify schizophrenia.

00:27:18.390 --> 00:27:21.150
And also, this is
all in research.

00:27:21.150 --> 00:27:23.970
It's not that in a
practical application, yet.

00:27:23.970 --> 00:27:27.780
We are trying to find the
gene for schizophrenia.

00:27:27.780 --> 00:27:31.380
So what we are doing is that
the National Institute of Mental

00:27:31.380 --> 00:27:36.130
Health supports us to collect
200 families in which two

00:27:36.130 --> 00:27:37.440
or more are affected.

00:27:37.440 --> 00:27:40.620
And we interview all
of the family members,

00:27:40.620 --> 00:27:42.390
and then we collect the DNA.

00:27:42.390 --> 00:27:46.740
And nationally, we are
collecting another 200.

00:27:46.740 --> 00:27:50.160
And then, from there,
we like to study,

00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:53.910
what are the potential genes.

00:27:53.910 --> 00:27:57.060
We already know there is no
one gene for schizophrenia.

00:27:57.060 --> 00:28:03.470
There must be many genes to
interact with the environment

00:28:03.470 --> 00:28:04.340
to develop.

00:28:04.340 --> 00:28:07.100
And not only that,
what we are studying

00:28:07.100 --> 00:28:11.260
is the subthreshold
of schizophrenia.

00:28:11.260 --> 00:28:13.290
It's called schizotaxia.

00:28:13.290 --> 00:28:14.875
In Paul Meehl's term.

00:28:17.540 --> 00:28:20.480
Essentially, those who have not
developed schizophrenia yet,

00:28:20.480 --> 00:28:28.090
but they have a tendency to
inherit schizophrenia, a trait.

00:28:28.090 --> 00:28:30.730
And using the
neuropsychological, cognitive

00:28:30.730 --> 00:28:33.940
deficit, and MRI family
study of schizophrenia,

00:28:33.940 --> 00:28:37.270
we are tackling that
what is that genotype

00:28:37.270 --> 00:28:42.100
and what is the phenotype
of schizophrenia.

00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:45.310
So the current concept is this.

00:28:45.310 --> 00:28:48.720
It's a vulnerability
with a genetic

00:28:48.720 --> 00:28:51.420
or the intra-uterine
abnormalities

00:28:51.420 --> 00:28:53.130
with a stress model.

00:28:53.130 --> 00:28:57.960
And if the stress is-- the
environmental risk factors--

00:28:57.960 --> 00:29:01.320
is higher, then it
becomes schizophrenia.

00:29:01.320 --> 00:29:04.140
And if not, it's a
subthreshold called

00:29:04.140 --> 00:29:08.190
spectrum disorders of this kind,
and genetic predisposition.

00:29:08.190 --> 00:29:13.170
So this is pretty much to
summarize the current theory

00:29:13.170 --> 00:29:14.040
of schizophrenia.

00:29:14.040 --> 00:29:17.610
We have not found one gene
for schizophrenia yet.

00:29:17.610 --> 00:29:20.520
We know there are
several genes involved.

00:29:23.120 --> 00:29:27.710
So essentially, to
summarize current finding

00:29:27.710 --> 00:29:30.410
of the concept of
schizophrenia, before I

00:29:30.410 --> 00:29:35.210
move into spirituality,
is that schizophrenia,

00:29:35.210 --> 00:29:40.100
from ancient, biblical
teachings, all considered

00:29:40.100 --> 00:29:43.140
to be possessed by the devil.

00:29:43.140 --> 00:29:45.750
But now, with the
scientific approach,

00:29:45.750 --> 00:29:48.930
neuroscience, we now
know schizophrenia is

00:29:48.930 --> 00:29:53.730
a disorder, mainly from brain.

00:29:53.730 --> 00:29:59.720
And it affects the thinking,
and feeling, and the behavior.

00:29:59.720 --> 00:30:03.930
And we now think,
our group, thinks

00:30:03.930 --> 00:30:08.180
that from available data, there
is a genetic predisposition.

00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:11.660
An early environmental
insult develops

00:30:11.660 --> 00:30:16.750
into the maldevelopment
of the brain.

00:30:16.750 --> 00:30:18.230
Particularly in cortex.

00:30:18.230 --> 00:30:21.680
And here, the doctor
[INAUDIBLE] here,

00:30:21.680 --> 00:30:24.125
in his hospital,
the McLean Hospital,

00:30:24.125 --> 00:30:32.320
they are actually analyzing
the brain neurons' arrangement

00:30:32.320 --> 00:30:33.040
in the cortex.

00:30:33.040 --> 00:30:35.950
And find the arrangement
on each layer

00:30:35.950 --> 00:30:43.640
seems to be not all
properly arranged,

00:30:43.640 --> 00:30:46.350
in comparing with normal.

00:30:46.350 --> 00:30:48.810
So it's the neural
developmental abnormalities.

00:30:48.810 --> 00:30:54.020
And the later environmental
insult. Particularly at the

00:30:54.020 --> 00:30:54.960
addresses.

00:30:54.960 --> 00:30:57.260
These are all present,
but they're silent.

00:30:57.260 --> 00:30:59.930
And later, particularly
at the teen age,

00:30:59.930 --> 00:31:07.280
or adolescence period, where
neurons, the brain growth,

00:31:07.280 --> 00:31:11.230
and the external
environmental insult,

00:31:11.230 --> 00:31:16.940
essentially result in, the brain
cannot react to the demands

00:31:16.940 --> 00:31:17.900
of the environment.

00:31:17.900 --> 00:31:20.870
Because the brain
is already abnormal.

00:31:20.870 --> 00:31:26.030
And then, followed up with brain
dysfunction and schizophrenia.

00:31:26.030 --> 00:31:29.630
And then, schizophrenia
causing psychosis.

00:31:29.630 --> 00:31:32.780
Psychosis, by that meaning,
these cerebral functions

00:31:32.780 --> 00:31:34.250
become incongruous.

00:31:34.250 --> 00:31:36.470
And then, hearing voices.

00:31:36.470 --> 00:31:40.940
And then, can hear
own thoughts aloud.

00:31:40.940 --> 00:31:44.900
Or they have many,
many bizarre delusions

00:31:44.900 --> 00:31:47.585
related to many things.

00:31:51.830 --> 00:31:57.270
And in the past, when we don't
know the satellite function,

00:31:57.270 --> 00:32:00.920
some of the patients
already believe that, oh,

00:32:00.920 --> 00:32:05.540
I can travel to other universe.

00:32:05.540 --> 00:32:08.350
And but now, seems to be real.

00:32:08.350 --> 00:32:11.040
So that is no longer
the delusions.

00:32:11.040 --> 00:32:14.150
So delusions, the definition
has to be interpreted

00:32:14.150 --> 00:32:16.070
from the cultural context.

00:32:16.070 --> 00:32:19.880
So the important part is this.

00:32:19.880 --> 00:32:24.550
If schizophrenia develops,
psychosis develops,

00:32:24.550 --> 00:32:27.940
it triggers the current theory.

00:32:27.940 --> 00:32:32.460
It triggers potentially becoming
the neural degeneration.

00:32:32.460 --> 00:32:34.090
There is no evidence yet.

00:32:34.090 --> 00:32:37.360
But that we know if a
schizophrenic psychosis

00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:43.410
episode develops, first
episode you don't treat.

00:32:43.410 --> 00:32:45.790
Then, second episode,
third episode.

00:32:45.790 --> 00:32:48.470
Then it is very
difficult to treat.

00:32:48.470 --> 00:32:56.790
So current emphasis is on how to
prevent the onset of psychosis.

00:32:56.790 --> 00:32:59.880
And at the Massachusetts
Mental Health Center,

00:32:59.880 --> 00:33:03.220
we are trying to develop
the prevention center

00:33:03.220 --> 00:33:07.110
and now it is not just to treat.

00:33:07.110 --> 00:33:11.280
We are trying to develop
a prevention strategy,

00:33:11.280 --> 00:33:18.970
both from biological and the
environmental point of view.

00:33:18.970 --> 00:33:21.690
So once it was a myth.

00:33:21.690 --> 00:33:24.190
Now, we understand the brain.

00:33:24.190 --> 00:33:30.910
And with an NIH effort,
called Decade of Brain,

00:33:30.910 --> 00:33:35.410
lots of efforts
are being utilized

00:33:35.410 --> 00:33:38.560
to study the brain
of schizophrenia,

00:33:38.560 --> 00:33:41.240
and affective
disorders, and others.

00:33:41.240 --> 00:33:48.910
So this is just to give you some
of the current study on brain

00:33:48.910 --> 00:33:49.990
and mind.

00:33:49.990 --> 00:33:55.310
Now with this background,
with spirituality.

00:33:55.310 --> 00:33:57.710
We are like in the old days.

00:33:57.710 --> 00:34:01.970
Spirituality is a
myth, and spirituality

00:34:01.970 --> 00:34:06.960
is the superstitious concept.

00:34:06.960 --> 00:34:11.610
In particular at MIT, where
they are all so reasonable.

00:34:11.610 --> 00:34:13.010
All so logic.

00:34:13.010 --> 00:34:19.210
So spirituality, when you
talk about it, it is a myth.

00:34:19.210 --> 00:34:21.699
It is the superstition.

00:34:21.699 --> 00:34:26.260
But schizophrenia, the reason
I use schizophrenia, was this.

00:34:26.260 --> 00:34:30.100
That in the past, schizophrenia
considered to be a myth.

00:34:30.100 --> 00:34:35.290
But that with the scientific
approach of the neuroscience,

00:34:35.290 --> 00:34:37.179
we are able to tackle them.

00:34:37.179 --> 00:34:39.969
Now we consider this
to be treatable.

00:34:39.969 --> 00:34:42.280
And if we can
clone the genes, we

00:34:42.280 --> 00:34:47.540
will be able to develop the
real treatment, and prevention,

00:34:47.540 --> 00:34:48.170
and so on.

00:34:48.170 --> 00:34:51.130
So with this as a
basis, I'm now going

00:34:51.130 --> 00:34:54.730
to move into a very difficult
area of the spirituality.

00:34:54.730 --> 00:34:57.070
Particularly for
great scientists,

00:34:57.070 --> 00:35:00.940
like here at the MIT.

00:35:00.940 --> 00:35:04.300
I'm not saying that there are
no great scientists at Harvard.

00:35:04.300 --> 00:35:07.630
Because I'm just saying
that we are here, at MIT.

00:35:07.630 --> 00:35:17.960
[LAUGHTER] So forgive me eminent
professor coming from Harvard.

00:35:17.960 --> 00:35:19.130
Forgive me.

00:35:19.130 --> 00:35:24.290
Because we are
utilizing MIT's space.

00:35:24.290 --> 00:35:29.520
So the reason we couldn't
do schizophrenia research

00:35:29.520 --> 00:35:33.380
is that there was no definition.

00:35:33.380 --> 00:35:36.300
Definition is according
to professors definition.

00:35:36.300 --> 00:35:38.580
Professors say, this
is schizophrenia,

00:35:38.580 --> 00:35:41.820
when it was a Dark
Age of psychiatry.

00:35:41.820 --> 00:35:44.700
Now, we develop all
kinds of criteria,

00:35:44.700 --> 00:35:47.630
which we study internationally,
which I participate.

00:35:47.630 --> 00:35:50.790
And we do the long-term
follow-up and family studies.

00:35:50.790 --> 00:35:53.100
We already know
there are essentially

00:35:53.100 --> 00:35:57.540
good criteria for diagnoses, but
not necessarily for research.

00:35:57.540 --> 00:36:02.040
So now, we at least have
an operational definition

00:36:02.040 --> 00:36:03.360
of schizophrenia.

00:36:03.360 --> 00:36:08.520
In spirituality, I
was invited to NIH,

00:36:08.520 --> 00:36:12.150
to the alternative
medicines conference.

00:36:12.150 --> 00:36:17.670
And I ask-- there are
many, many experts there.

00:36:17.670 --> 00:36:20.650
I say, could you define for
me, what is spirituality?

00:36:20.650 --> 00:36:25.890
Apparently, a Dark
Age of psychiatry,

00:36:25.890 --> 00:36:30.090
where everyone has their own
definition of schizophrenia.

00:36:30.090 --> 00:36:32.340
Nowadays, we have
a common criteria.

00:36:32.340 --> 00:36:34.380
So it is important to
develop the criteria,

00:36:34.380 --> 00:36:38.110
before we're launching
into the spirituality.

00:36:38.110 --> 00:36:41.030
When you read in the magazine,
in the Time magazine,

00:36:41.030 --> 00:36:43.050
and the New York
Times, they are talking

00:36:43.050 --> 00:36:47.610
about, if you pray more,
than your health is better.

00:36:47.610 --> 00:36:49.560
Those kind of things.

00:36:49.560 --> 00:36:53.840
We need to do rigorous research.

00:36:53.840 --> 00:36:56.820
I believe we cannot
do it completely.

00:36:56.820 --> 00:37:00.500
Like in schizophrenia,
we did it,

00:37:00.500 --> 00:37:03.380
but we only scratched
the surface.

00:37:03.380 --> 00:37:09.470
And I sort of feel that doing
research on spirituality

00:37:09.470 --> 00:37:13.020
is like doing
schizophrenia research

00:37:13.020 --> 00:37:16.130
in the Dark Age of psychiatry.

00:37:16.130 --> 00:37:20.990
And the operational
criteria is very important.

00:37:20.990 --> 00:37:27.550
To really tackle, is
spirituality related to health?

00:37:27.550 --> 00:37:31.860
Ill health, mentally,
or physically.

00:37:31.860 --> 00:37:37.070
And from my practice of
seeing patients, many patients

00:37:37.070 --> 00:37:43.100
in the past, seldom they talk
about the spiritual dimension.

00:37:43.100 --> 00:37:46.540
Now, if you ask
which denomination--

00:37:46.540 --> 00:37:48.800
which religion are
you affiliated with,

00:37:48.800 --> 00:37:49.880
they'll start to talk.

00:37:49.880 --> 00:37:51.710
Particularly for many patients.

00:37:51.710 --> 00:37:58.360
They like us to really
engage in the mind, brain,

00:37:58.360 --> 00:38:00.740
and spiritual dimensions.

00:38:00.740 --> 00:38:05.410
And if your patients
are interested in using

00:38:05.410 --> 00:38:09.910
the spirituality dimension
to help their illness, why

00:38:09.910 --> 00:38:11.000
should you deny them?

00:38:17.940 --> 00:38:19.110
You know that,

00:38:19.110 --> 00:38:23.940
From your own existence,
even though you

00:38:23.940 --> 00:38:26.030
don't know where the mind is--

00:38:26.030 --> 00:38:28.630
but now we know it is in brain.

00:38:28.630 --> 00:38:30.610
And we know the function.

00:38:30.610 --> 00:38:35.160
And because we operationalize,
what is a mental function.

00:38:35.160 --> 00:38:39.540
For the spirituality research
which we are now launching on,

00:38:39.540 --> 00:38:44.130
we have to have at least
some spiritual, operational

00:38:44.130 --> 00:38:45.430
definition.

00:38:45.430 --> 00:38:51.090
So this is not the definition
which I'm proposing.

00:38:51.090 --> 00:38:55.440
I'll just give you one example
of, you have to characterize,

00:38:55.440 --> 00:38:56.910
what is schizophrenia.

00:38:56.910 --> 00:38:59.370
In doing spirituality
research, we

00:38:59.370 --> 00:39:04.780
have to characterize
measurable spiritual dimension.

00:39:04.780 --> 00:39:06.970
I'm not saying that with
this, we can understand

00:39:06.970 --> 00:39:08.260
all the spirituality.

00:39:08.260 --> 00:39:10.870
Like in schizophrenia,
we characterize them,

00:39:10.870 --> 00:39:12.250
we understand the brain.

00:39:12.250 --> 00:39:16.950
Yet we still don't know many,
many aspects of schizophrenia.

00:39:16.950 --> 00:39:23.200
But at least that we can get to
some aspects of schizophrenia,

00:39:23.200 --> 00:39:24.520
like this.

00:39:24.520 --> 00:39:30.280
Our group now launching into
the spirituality research.

00:39:30.280 --> 00:39:33.730
And I'm going to give you some
of the spirituality research

00:39:33.730 --> 00:39:36.460
affecting the health,
which we are now

00:39:36.460 --> 00:39:38.750
contemplating to launch on.

00:39:38.750 --> 00:39:42.150
But before that, let us--

00:39:42.150 --> 00:39:44.180
how many minutes
do I still have?

00:39:44.180 --> 00:39:44.680
Tell me.

00:39:44.680 --> 00:39:46.150
PRESENTER: 15 to 20.

00:39:46.150 --> 00:39:46.980
TSUANG: 15 to 20.

00:39:46.980 --> 00:39:47.560
OK.

00:39:47.560 --> 00:39:53.290
So this, for me to organize
this very important aspect

00:39:53.290 --> 00:39:56.930
of this spirituality research.

00:39:56.930 --> 00:39:59.570
The participation in
organized religion,

00:39:59.570 --> 00:40:02.390
participation in non-organized
speech or activities,

00:40:02.390 --> 00:40:06.950
prayer and meditation,
read sacred scriptures,

00:40:06.950 --> 00:40:11.290
profess a relationship with
God, or an outward spirituality.

00:40:11.290 --> 00:40:16.390
Profess to believe in the
corporal spirit or soul.

00:40:16.390 --> 00:40:21.790
Gives unselfishly about
your time, and resources

00:40:21.790 --> 00:40:23.030
to help others.

00:40:23.030 --> 00:40:27.360
This is a very broad
definition of spirituality.

00:40:27.360 --> 00:40:30.040
So with this, if we
can characterize them,

00:40:30.040 --> 00:40:34.000
then we'll be able to use
the epidemiological technique

00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:37.240
to really study them.

00:40:37.240 --> 00:40:39.700
The current report-- I'm
not saying current reports

00:40:39.700 --> 00:40:41.290
are all wrong.

00:40:41.290 --> 00:40:46.540
They are tilted to a very
subjective interpretation

00:40:46.540 --> 00:40:49.180
of the result. Which
I'm going to emphasize.

00:40:49.180 --> 00:40:52.615
So we need to think about--

00:40:52.615 --> 00:40:56.470
in epidemiology you're always
thinking about the rate.

00:40:56.470 --> 00:41:00.890
The numerator, and denominator.

00:41:00.890 --> 00:41:03.010
So this is talking
about the denominator.

00:41:03.010 --> 00:41:06.490
When you talk of the rate of
those who pray versus those who

00:41:06.490 --> 00:41:09.850
do not pray, you have to
have, which population

00:41:09.850 --> 00:41:11.380
are you talking about.

00:41:11.380 --> 00:41:14.710
And then, operational
definition is the numerator.

00:41:14.710 --> 00:41:22.260
So here, in various
populations, whether you

00:41:22.260 --> 00:41:27.600
study children, teenagers, or
elderly, or severely mentally

00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:31.320
ill, or chronically
ill, or disabled,

00:41:31.320 --> 00:41:34.500
and economically
disadvantaged minorities,

00:41:34.500 --> 00:41:36.750
terminally ill, or dying--

00:41:36.750 --> 00:41:42.070
essentially just do a census
of, have you gone to church.

00:41:42.070 --> 00:41:45.190
And you don't know which kind
of population are you studying.

00:41:45.190 --> 00:41:47.110
You don't know the denominator.

00:41:47.110 --> 00:41:50.750
That is a problem of the
research in this area.

00:41:50.750 --> 00:41:53.700
So when we study
them, we need to--

00:41:53.700 --> 00:41:56.150
in schizophrenia, there
are several subtypes.

00:41:56.150 --> 00:41:58.270
We subtype them, and study them.

00:41:58.270 --> 00:42:03.140
Then we know how to
study efficiently.

00:42:03.140 --> 00:42:09.940
So the gender, some of them
never report what is the sex--

00:42:09.940 --> 00:42:11.890
what is the gender.

00:42:11.890 --> 00:42:14.830
And then report that you
do this, then this happens.

00:42:14.830 --> 00:42:18.850
That is all a very,
very erroneous approach

00:42:18.850 --> 00:42:21.550
to the study of spirituality.

00:42:21.550 --> 00:42:23.570
It is so difficult to study.

00:42:23.570 --> 00:42:27.250
Then if you mix
the denominators,

00:42:27.250 --> 00:42:29.770
then you are unable
to study them.

00:42:29.770 --> 00:42:32.981
Then what religion, education,
socioeconomic status.

00:42:32.981 --> 00:42:34.480
When you read in
the New York Times,

00:42:34.480 --> 00:42:35.950
they talk about
the various kinds.

00:42:35.950 --> 00:42:39.640
And seldom they
characterize the denominator

00:42:39.640 --> 00:42:44.810
from which the
population are drawn.

00:42:44.810 --> 00:42:47.440
And then, the
operational definition

00:42:47.440 --> 00:42:52.330
of the spirituality, this
is a very important aspect

00:42:52.330 --> 00:42:54.520
of epidemiology, in
which I'm specializing.

00:42:54.520 --> 00:42:56.380
The mind is a
psychiatric epidemiology.

00:42:56.380 --> 00:43:00.280
Meaning studying the mind,
and the function of the mind.

00:43:00.280 --> 00:43:04.690
Then we use that
technique to see

00:43:04.690 --> 00:43:07.750
if we can operationalize
spirituality

00:43:07.750 --> 00:43:09.260
to a certain extent.

00:43:09.260 --> 00:43:11.650
I'm not saying perfect,
like schizophrenia.

00:43:11.650 --> 00:43:14.710
We have operational
criteria to study brain.

00:43:14.710 --> 00:43:18.010
We now need to study
our spirituality

00:43:18.010 --> 00:43:23.110
using a similar technique.

00:43:23.110 --> 00:43:28.300
And then, another
deficit is that, in some

00:43:28.300 --> 00:43:31.240
of the report which
you read, they seldom

00:43:31.240 --> 00:43:33.190
have a control group.

00:43:33.190 --> 00:43:35.230
There is no comparison group.

00:43:35.230 --> 00:43:36.730
They just study them.

00:43:36.730 --> 00:43:40.410
It is not going to get anywhere.

00:43:40.410 --> 00:43:49.930
So the control group to
examine placebo effect, this

00:43:49.930 --> 00:43:51.570
is difficult to study.

00:43:51.570 --> 00:43:55.510
But we can design it
with a comparison group

00:43:55.510 --> 00:43:58.990
to study, what is
the placebo effect.

00:43:58.990 --> 00:44:03.070
So in addition to
that, you say improve.

00:44:03.070 --> 00:44:03.800
What is improve?

00:44:06.340 --> 00:44:11.120
There is no criteria
for outcome.

00:44:11.120 --> 00:44:13.270
So it is difficult
to characterize them.

00:44:13.270 --> 00:44:17.410
You need to study
the physical health,

00:44:17.410 --> 00:44:19.180
and then characterize them.

00:44:19.180 --> 00:44:24.020
In heart disease, cancer,
or mortality, mental health,

00:44:24.020 --> 00:44:28.660
psychiatric diagnosis, substance
abuse, and the helplessness,

00:44:28.660 --> 00:44:31.090
hopelessness, and coping style.

00:44:31.090 --> 00:44:34.150
And various kinds
of suicide attempts.

00:44:34.150 --> 00:44:38.000
And more importantly,
the marital status,

00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:39.580
socioeconomic status.

00:44:39.580 --> 00:44:41.100
Apparently, focus is not good.

00:44:45.300 --> 00:44:47.380
Can you focus a little bit?

00:44:47.380 --> 00:44:48.330
It's all right.

00:44:48.330 --> 00:44:54.090
The educational outcome
and arrest and conviction.

00:44:54.090 --> 00:44:54.590
OK.

00:44:54.590 --> 00:44:55.100
That's fine.

00:44:55.100 --> 00:44:55.950
Thank you.

00:44:55.950 --> 00:44:58.700
Thank you very much.

00:44:58.700 --> 00:45:05.180
So outcome has to be
assessed, in order

00:45:05.180 --> 00:45:09.710
to study the spirituality
and its impact

00:45:09.710 --> 00:45:13.320
on health, physical
and mental health.

00:45:13.320 --> 00:45:16.850
So this assessment
has to be reliable.

00:45:16.850 --> 00:45:20.270
You need to develop
the assessment form.

00:45:20.270 --> 00:45:24.710
And which test, and retest,
reliability of the assessment.

00:45:24.710 --> 00:45:27.920
And then, train people
to really come up

00:45:27.920 --> 00:45:30.500
with a reliable
assessment of outcome.

00:45:30.500 --> 00:45:34.190
And this outcome has to
have-- it's not just reliable.

00:45:34.190 --> 00:45:36.740
It has to have its validity.

00:45:36.740 --> 00:45:39.740
And it has to be objective,
and standardized.

00:45:39.740 --> 00:45:42.350
And when you are
interviewing, by comparing

00:45:42.350 --> 00:45:45.710
the control group and
the experimental group,

00:45:45.710 --> 00:45:48.040
it has to be blind

00:45:48.040 --> 00:45:50.470
When we study
schizophrenia relatives,

00:45:50.470 --> 00:45:53.690
we don't know what kind of
relatives are we studying.

00:45:53.690 --> 00:45:56.620
This kind of a modern
epidemiological technique

00:45:56.620 --> 00:45:58.970
has to be utilized.

00:45:58.970 --> 00:46:05.820
So the epidemiological
study, we tend

00:46:05.820 --> 00:46:07.860
to jump to cause and effect.

00:46:07.860 --> 00:46:09.850
In schizophrenia,
in the beginning,

00:46:09.850 --> 00:46:12.720
we thought that there's a
cause and effect relationship.

00:46:12.720 --> 00:46:15.930
We don't know there
is a cause, one cause.

00:46:15.930 --> 00:46:17.640
We know the risk factors.

00:46:17.640 --> 00:46:22.850
Using the same analogy that,
if there is an evidence that

00:46:22.850 --> 00:46:26.000
spirituality is associated
with improved health outcome,

00:46:26.000 --> 00:46:29.280
we'll want to know whether
there is a cause and effect

00:46:29.280 --> 00:46:30.510
relationship.

00:46:30.510 --> 00:46:31.650
Cause and effect.

00:46:31.650 --> 00:46:34.380
Spirituality leads to
lower levels of anxiety,

00:46:34.380 --> 00:46:39.045
versus association,
spirituality and low anxiety

00:46:39.045 --> 00:46:41.180
are actually intertwined.

00:46:41.180 --> 00:46:43.730
Related with the correlation.

00:46:43.730 --> 00:46:45.600
So cause and effect, we--

00:46:45.600 --> 00:46:49.590
so usually it's the
published paper,

00:46:49.590 --> 00:46:55.400
or the newspaper talking about,
it's usually the correlation.

00:46:55.400 --> 00:46:59.840
It's not the cause and effect,
and written in such a way

00:46:59.840 --> 00:47:01.940
to mislead people.

00:47:01.940 --> 00:47:07.370
To really think that there is a
cause and effect relationship.

00:47:07.370 --> 00:47:10.110
And then, the cause
and effect, it

00:47:10.110 --> 00:47:13.110
is helpful to classify
the concept of cause.

00:47:13.110 --> 00:47:16.160
Traditional concept
of unnecessary cause.

00:47:16.160 --> 00:47:19.130
And the traditional concept
of sufficient cause.

00:47:19.130 --> 00:47:22.280
An epidemiological concept,
of contributory cause.

00:47:22.280 --> 00:47:24.035
Those need to be applied.

00:47:27.090 --> 00:47:30.780
And essentially, in
complex situations

00:47:30.780 --> 00:47:33.450
with many contributing
factors, one also

00:47:33.450 --> 00:47:35.850
needs to consider
supportive criteria

00:47:35.850 --> 00:47:37.650
for a contributory cause.

00:47:37.650 --> 00:47:39.900
Strength and consistency
of the association

00:47:39.900 --> 00:47:42.200
between spirituality
and health outcome.

00:47:42.200 --> 00:47:45.530
And if this is
biologically plausible.

00:47:45.530 --> 00:47:46.810
That is important.

00:47:46.810 --> 00:47:49.850
And evidence of relationship
between increased spirituality

00:47:49.850 --> 00:47:53.460
and better health outcomes.

00:47:53.460 --> 00:47:57.080
And the interpretation
of the result.

00:47:57.080 --> 00:47:59.510
Could not be a
subjective, should

00:47:59.510 --> 00:48:03.090
be based on the evidence.

00:48:03.090 --> 00:48:05.780
And the extrapolation
to a new population.

00:48:05.780 --> 00:48:09.830
Once you find the new finding
of the spirituality and health

00:48:09.830 --> 00:48:14.270
relationship, you need to apply
it to another denominator,

00:48:14.270 --> 00:48:18.770
and to see if it
could be generatable.

00:48:18.770 --> 00:48:24.640
So I'll just give you one
example of what we have,

00:48:24.640 --> 00:48:28.000
and what we are beginning to do.

00:48:28.000 --> 00:48:32.560
It is my personal conviction,
from my own practice,

00:48:32.560 --> 00:48:38.620
and my own personal belief, that
spiritual dimension is there.

00:48:38.620 --> 00:48:43.840
And I believe that, with the
rigorous current research

00:48:43.840 --> 00:48:46.810
methodology which we
use for schizophrenia,

00:48:46.810 --> 00:48:50.680
we can apply to
study spirituality

00:48:50.680 --> 00:48:53.620
and its relationship
with health.

00:48:53.620 --> 00:48:56.490
Particularly, with mental
health, which is my area.

00:48:56.490 --> 00:49:01.400
And I witness that the
patient, one to one,

00:49:01.400 --> 00:49:05.900
spirituality affects
the patients very much.

00:49:05.900 --> 00:49:10.480
Particularly in drug abuse,
in the depression, and so on.

00:49:10.480 --> 00:49:15.880
So we now have the huge
sample of the twins,

00:49:15.880 --> 00:49:18.760
about 4,000 twin pairs.

00:49:18.760 --> 00:49:22.150
And the conceptual
model is this.

00:49:25.590 --> 00:49:32.890
Essentially, here we have
concordant, monozygotic twins.

00:49:32.890 --> 00:49:33.790
All right?

00:49:33.790 --> 00:49:37.580
And if we develop
a speech of scale,

00:49:37.580 --> 00:49:42.160
the mean score, and then this
is very difficult to see,

00:49:42.160 --> 00:49:44.810
because I simplified it.

00:49:44.810 --> 00:49:50.290
But I will use a few minutes
to elaborate this to conclude.

00:49:50.290 --> 00:49:53.740
This is what I reported to
the National Institute of Drug

00:49:53.740 --> 00:49:55.930
Abuse to study them.

00:49:55.930 --> 00:50:01.080
Essentially, the
identical twins, they

00:50:01.080 --> 00:50:04.020
share all the genes in common.

00:50:04.020 --> 00:50:07.050
And what becomes
different is that there's

00:50:07.050 --> 00:50:13.690
some other factors, which
is not genetics, affecting

00:50:13.690 --> 00:50:17.450
the concordance or discordance.

00:50:17.450 --> 00:50:22.550
Concordance meaning,
that both identical twins

00:50:22.550 --> 00:50:26.630
are non-abusers.

00:50:26.630 --> 00:50:28.580
Never abused drugs.

00:50:28.580 --> 00:50:32.090
Never been diagnosed
as the drug abuse.

00:50:32.090 --> 00:50:37.880
Then the abuser, are those,
both identical twins in the pair

00:50:37.880 --> 00:50:39.980
are drug abusers.

00:50:39.980 --> 00:50:45.710
And discordant meaning, that
one twin, monozygotic, identical

00:50:45.710 --> 00:50:52.550
twin, is non-abuser, and
another one is abuser.

00:50:52.550 --> 00:50:53.210
OK?

00:50:53.210 --> 00:51:00.550
So the inference here is
that, if you are both abusers,

00:51:00.550 --> 00:51:02.960
then control for
genetics makeup.

00:51:02.960 --> 00:51:06.560
And the mean score
of spirituality,

00:51:06.560 --> 00:51:11.050
hypothesis which I would like
to test, should be the lowest.

00:51:11.050 --> 00:51:13.750
And the concordant
one, in the middle.

00:51:13.750 --> 00:51:20.620
Then discordant twins, who share
the same genetic makeup, yet

00:51:20.620 --> 00:51:22.630
this person is non-abuser.

00:51:22.630 --> 00:51:27.610
And this person says,
spirituality score is high.

00:51:27.610 --> 00:51:32.440
So essentially, if spirituality
is a protective factor,

00:51:32.440 --> 00:51:36.160
abusers should score
relatively low on spirituality.

00:51:36.160 --> 00:51:39.910
Non-abusing members of pairs,
concordant for non-abuse,

00:51:39.910 --> 00:51:42.680
that is low risk subject,
have spirituality

00:51:42.680 --> 00:51:44.680
score intermediate.

00:51:44.680 --> 00:51:48.070
Between abusers and non-abusers
from discordant pairs.

00:51:48.070 --> 00:51:50.290
Because non-abusers
from discord pairs

00:51:50.290 --> 00:51:53.290
which have a high
spirituality scores

00:51:53.290 --> 00:51:57.670
are assumed to be at
high risk for drug abuse.

00:51:57.670 --> 00:52:00.040
The absence of abuse
suggests the presence

00:52:00.040 --> 00:52:02.740
of a protective
spirituality factor.

00:52:02.740 --> 00:52:06.040
I'm just talking about one
way of approaching them.

00:52:06.040 --> 00:52:09.120
Then another dimension
of the spirituality,

00:52:09.120 --> 00:52:13.330
which Templeton's Foundation
is very interested in,

00:52:13.330 --> 00:52:20.440
is how to tie the spirituality
dimension about thankfulness,

00:52:20.440 --> 00:52:26.450
and forgiveness, to relate
it to physical health.

00:52:26.450 --> 00:52:28.400
And the mental health.

00:52:28.400 --> 00:52:31.420
So we now are
collecting the twins

00:52:31.420 --> 00:52:33.415
who served in the Vietnam--

00:52:36.100 --> 00:52:40.350
Vietnam veterans.

00:52:40.350 --> 00:52:43.950
Served in the Vietnam
combat theater.

00:52:43.950 --> 00:52:46.540
And some of them, identical
twins, both are there.

00:52:46.540 --> 00:52:49.850
Some of them, both are in the
continental United States.

00:52:49.850 --> 00:52:52.960
They total, 4,000 pairs.

00:52:52.960 --> 00:52:56.980
We can study their
post-traumatic disorders.

00:52:56.980 --> 00:52:59.650
Post-traumatic stress
disorder in the combat.

00:52:59.650 --> 00:53:02.100
You see your friend die.

00:53:02.100 --> 00:53:05.050
And why some of them
are still thankful?

00:53:05.050 --> 00:53:07.180
And why some of them are bitter?

00:53:07.180 --> 00:53:10.030
And we can control
for the environment,

00:53:10.030 --> 00:53:12.530
and the genetic
makeup, to study them.

00:53:12.530 --> 00:53:15.580
So in a nutshell, what
I'm saying is this.

00:53:15.580 --> 00:53:17.440
It is difficult to
study spirituality.

00:53:17.440 --> 00:53:21.720
And I have to confess that we
cannot understand spirituality

00:53:21.720 --> 00:53:26.050
fully, but that
spirituality is there.

00:53:26.050 --> 00:53:30.520
And that, if we think that
we are just a brain and mind,

00:53:30.520 --> 00:53:33.160
you are underestimating
yourself.

00:53:33.160 --> 00:53:35.310
There is a spiritual dimension.

00:53:35.310 --> 00:53:40.600
Love, and the
thankfulness, forgiveness.

00:53:40.600 --> 00:53:44.470
Those are considered to be
a very important, vital part

00:53:44.470 --> 00:53:45.920
of spirituality.

00:53:45.920 --> 00:53:48.220
So like the
schizophrenia research,

00:53:48.220 --> 00:53:53.380
if we can tie this together,
at least from epidemiological,

00:53:53.380 --> 00:53:58.090
risk factors design, we'll
be able to characterize them.

00:53:58.090 --> 00:54:00.790
Then later, it's not a dream.

00:54:00.790 --> 00:54:05.140
Now with the neuroimaging,
with the brain abnormality,

00:54:05.140 --> 00:54:06.910
which we can
characterize them, we

00:54:06.910 --> 00:54:10.960
may be able to find that at
those areas I'm dreaming,

00:54:10.960 --> 00:54:14.710
those areas which actually
expresses thankfulness,

00:54:14.710 --> 00:54:15.800
or forgiveness.

00:54:15.800 --> 00:54:19.220
Like the Vietnam era.

00:54:19.220 --> 00:54:23.920
Being killed, friend being
killed by Vietnamese, and still

00:54:23.920 --> 00:54:25.750
now can't forget.

00:54:25.750 --> 00:54:27.880
Those kinds of
tendencies are actually

00:54:27.880 --> 00:54:31.810
very much about genetics and
environmental interaction.

00:54:31.810 --> 00:54:34.900
We now know that the--

00:54:34.900 --> 00:54:39.380
you may not believe it-- the
data, if you characterize well,

00:54:39.380 --> 00:54:46.990
spirituality has the familial
and the genetic tendencies.

00:54:46.990 --> 00:54:50.110
But not all genetics,
Shared environment

00:54:50.110 --> 00:54:51.980
is also very important.

00:54:51.980 --> 00:54:56.530
So in conclusion, what
I'm saying is that,

00:54:56.530 --> 00:55:00.940
doing schizophrenia
for the last 35 years,

00:55:00.940 --> 00:55:04.070
I'm personally convinced
that spirituality,

00:55:04.070 --> 00:55:08.890
which is my personal
belief, with the existence

00:55:08.890 --> 00:55:10.720
of the spirituality.

00:55:10.720 --> 00:55:16.030
I'd really like to tackle
this very difficult subject.

00:55:16.030 --> 00:55:18.130
Do it properly.

00:55:18.130 --> 00:55:21.260
And then, we'll be able to
understand the mind, brain,

00:55:21.260 --> 00:55:23.650
and spirituality.

00:55:23.650 --> 00:55:24.647
My time is up.

00:55:24.647 --> 00:55:25.480
Thank you very much.

00:55:25.480 --> 00:55:37.230
