00:56:38.720 --> 00:56:39.220
population.

00:56:39.220 --> 00:56:39.720
Yes.

00:56:42.840 --> 00:56:45.490
AUDIENCE: Getting back to
schizophrenia for a minute.

00:56:45.490 --> 00:56:45.990
TSUANG: Yes.

00:56:45.990 --> 00:56:49.370
AUDIENCE: You showed that it's
a form of a structural defect

00:56:49.370 --> 00:56:50.602
in the brain.

00:56:50.602 --> 00:56:52.510
At the same time,
I guess it's known,

00:56:52.510 --> 00:56:55.720
I think that it usually
onsets in the teenage time.

00:56:55.720 --> 00:56:58.480
And you also said that
it comes in episodes.

00:56:58.480 --> 00:57:00.920
So if it's a
structural defect, why

00:57:00.920 --> 00:57:05.166
does it have this specific
onset and episodic behavior?

00:57:05.166 --> 00:57:08.403
TSUANG: That is a fact
that we are really

00:57:08.403 --> 00:57:09.660
trying to understand.

00:57:09.660 --> 00:57:13.980
And this has been a very,
very important question.

00:57:13.980 --> 00:57:19.280
Why having this maldevelopment
already there, at the birth,

00:57:19.280 --> 00:57:24.620
and why it do not to
have an onset very early.

00:57:24.620 --> 00:57:28.220
And usually occurs
from the age 15,

00:57:28.220 --> 00:57:31.130
16, that is, a teenage period.

00:57:31.130 --> 00:57:35.120
The current theory is this, that
the brain development has not

00:57:35.120 --> 00:57:37.160
matured yet.

00:57:37.160 --> 00:57:39.900
Until the teenage.

00:57:39.900 --> 00:57:43.310
And when, in the
adolescent period,

00:57:43.310 --> 00:57:45.480
there are demands
from the environment.

00:57:45.480 --> 00:57:47.450
Brain's demands
from the environment

00:57:47.450 --> 00:57:49.560
become heavier and heavier.

00:57:49.560 --> 00:57:53.120
And at that time, all
the maturity of the brain

00:57:53.120 --> 00:57:55.290
actually accomplishes
at that time.

00:57:55.290 --> 00:57:59.350
In schizophrenia brain, it
has not been accomplished.

00:57:59.350 --> 00:58:06.590
That immature brain cannot cope
with the environmental stress.

00:58:06.590 --> 00:58:09.680
So usually, that is the time.

00:58:09.680 --> 00:58:12.380
Because the brain
is so inefficient,

00:58:12.380 --> 00:58:16.070
then to respond to
the environment,

00:58:16.070 --> 00:58:17.550
it cannot function.

00:58:17.550 --> 00:58:19.430
Therefore, develops
the symptoms.

00:58:19.430 --> 00:58:23.470
That is a current theory.

00:58:23.470 --> 00:58:28.130
An episode is, when you
don't treat a psychosis,

00:58:28.130 --> 00:58:31.400
psychosis may become
the triggering

00:58:31.400 --> 00:58:34.520
effect for another episode.

00:58:34.520 --> 00:58:36.710
So it needs to be treated.

00:58:36.710 --> 00:58:39.350
So our current approach
is, how to find

00:58:39.350 --> 00:58:44.240
those children who have not
developed schizophrenia, yet.

00:58:44.240 --> 00:58:46.880
Yet we know there are
genetic risk factors,

00:58:46.880 --> 00:58:50.480
and environmental factors, with
the brain imaging abnormality.

00:58:50.480 --> 00:58:53.610
How to help them not
become schizophrenic.

00:58:53.610 --> 00:58:57.170
So schizophrenia research is
now moving into prevention mode.

00:58:57.170 --> 00:58:59.470
It is a cutting
edge of research.

00:58:59.470 --> 00:59:01.410
Not in everywhere, yet.

00:59:01.410 --> 00:59:02.145
Yes?

