Some of which is actually
at [INAUDIBLE] MIT.

01:04:56.640 --> 01:04:59.010
Are you aware of
studies of the sort

01:04:59.010 --> 01:05:03.530
of neurological differences
between, let's say,

01:05:03.530 --> 01:05:07.454
experienced meditators, and
non-meditators, or people who

01:05:07.454 --> 01:05:09.744
might be considered to
be highly spiritual,

01:05:09.744 --> 01:05:11.009
and others who are not?

01:05:11.009 --> 01:05:12.550
TSUANG: Yeah, there
are lots reports.

01:05:12.550 --> 01:05:16.670
But for me, to really
say that is credible,

01:05:16.670 --> 01:05:20.420
to meet the criteria, which
actually illustrates it.

01:05:20.420 --> 01:05:27.560
So I have not come up with a
good study which I can quote.

01:05:27.560 --> 01:05:29.420
So sorry, I don't have.

01:05:29.420 --> 01:05:31.360
Yeah, there are
several publications.

01:05:31.360 --> 01:05:35.120
But if you use the
epidemiological approach

01:05:35.120 --> 01:05:40.240
to that, those are,
should I say, shaky.

01:05:40.240 --> 01:05:40.750
Shaky.

01:05:40.750 --> 01:05:44.010
Because the use of the
denominator and the numerator

01:05:44.010 --> 01:05:48.670
are not in accordance
with our criteria.

01:05:48.670 --> 01:05:51.820
But on the personal
level, one to one,

01:05:51.820 --> 01:05:54.940
I'm talking about the
application to everyone.

01:05:54.940 --> 01:05:56.440
To the huge population.

01:05:56.440 --> 01:05:58.420
That is what
epidemiology is doing.

01:05:58.420 --> 01:06:01.360
But person to person,
if you talk to a person,

01:06:01.360 --> 01:06:04.780
they firmly believe that
the mind meditation actually

01:06:04.780 --> 01:06:08.500
affects my physical well-being.

01:06:08.500 --> 01:06:12.100
And if he say that,
who are you to deny

01:06:12.100 --> 01:06:15.350
that he doesn't feel that?

01:06:15.350 --> 01:06:15.860
No.

01:06:15.860 --> 01:06:20.770
Individually, my patient tells
me, after you talked to me,

01:06:20.770 --> 01:06:25.990
and you say, prayer
me help in my first--

01:06:25.990 --> 01:06:27.880
I was a Catholic.

01:06:27.880 --> 01:06:32.440
But I never went to any church.

01:06:32.440 --> 01:06:34.900
But now I'm depressed.

01:06:34.900 --> 01:06:37.590
Then, I start to pray.

01:06:37.590 --> 01:06:40.530
And, lo and behold,
I feel better.

01:06:40.530 --> 01:06:44.650
Whether it's a placebo effect
or not, individual case.

01:06:44.650 --> 01:06:48.030
So we have to divide the
individual dimension,

01:06:48.030 --> 01:06:50.670
and the whole epidemiological.

01:06:50.670 --> 01:06:56.780
So one to one, who am I to
deny this patient's statement

01:06:56.780 --> 01:06:59.090
of his condition?

01:06:59.090 --> 01:07:01.540
I cannot.

01:07:01.540 --> 01:07:05.451
That is the important
things to differentiate.

01:07:05.451 --> 01:07:07.200
PRESENTER: Unfortunately,
we have to stop.

01:07:07.200 --> 01:07:12.020
[APPLAUSE]

01:07:12.020 --> 01:07:12.770
TSUANG: Thank you.

01:07:12.770 --> 01:07:13.603
Thank you very much.

01:07:13.603 --> 01:07:15.620
PRESENTER: Thank you
so much for coming.

01:07:15.620 --> 01:07:18.070
That was wonderful.

